# M24.4 item 1 -- TTC-rate-vs-virtual-time gate. Must pass before anything else in M24.4 is
# trusted (task brief: "Do item 1 first -- everything else depends on it").
#
# Loads RTEMS's own `ticker` sample (the same M24.2/M24.2d artifact,
# third_party/rtems-container/run-renode/ticker.exe -- reused read-only, not rebuilt here)
# on rpu0, but against AltaVista's OWN platform file
# (third_party/renode/platforms/cpus/zynqmp.repl, this file's sibling) instead of Renode's
# shipped one, so `ttc0`'s `frequency: 100000000` line is in effect. `ticker` is used (not
# `hello`) because `hello` explicitly disables the RTEMS clock driver
# (CONFIGURE_APPLICATION_DOES_NOT_NEED_CLOCK_DRIVER) and never programs TTC0's CNT_CNTRL, so
# its COUNT_VALUE would never move -- there would be nothing to measure a rate against.
#
# Modeled on third_party/rtems-container/run-renode/ticker_noquit.resc (same reset macro,
# same ELF, same "no RunFor/quit here -- the driving script owns stepping" convention) with
# exactly one change: LoadPlatformDescription points at our own .repl by absolute path, not
# the shipped `@platforms/cpus/zynqmp.repl` search-path form. An absolute path after `@` is
# already a literal string needing no `$ORIGIN` substitution, so it does not hit the
# `@$ORIGIN/...`-suppresses-substitution bug M24.2b found and recorded in hello.resc's own
# comment.

:name: av-m24-4-ttc-rate-test

using sysbus
using sysbus.cluster0
using sysbus.cluster1

mach create "av-m24-4-ttc-rate-test"

machine LoadPlatformDescription @/Users/probe/code/AltaVista/third_party/renode/platforms/cpus/zynqmp.repl

uart0 CreateFileBackend $ORIGIN/ttc_rate_uart.log true

macro reset
"""
    cluster0 ForEach IsHalted true
    cluster1 ForEach IsHalted true
    rpu0 IsHalted false

    sysbus LoadELF @/Users/probe/code/AltaVista/third_party/rtems-container/run-renode/ticker.exe cpu=rpu0
"""

runMacro $reset
